    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-p1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "By rationalising the numerator, show that the difference quotient is equal to $$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x}}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x}}$\n\nMultiply by the conjugate of the numerator to obtain a factor of $h$ that cancels.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{x+h}-\\sqrt{x}}{h}\\\\\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}&=\\frac{(\\sqrt{x+h}-\\sqrt{x})(\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x})}{h(\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x})}\\\\\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}&=\\frac{(x+h)-x}{h(\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x})}\\\\\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x)}{h}&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-p1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, write down what $f'(x)$ is.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}$ for $x>0$.",
          "worked": "For $x>0$, $$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+h}+\\sqrt{x}}\\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 22
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-p1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Use a similar technique to calculate $f'(x)$ if $f(x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$f'(x)=-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{x}}$ for $x>0$.\n\nCombine the reciprocals and rationalise the resulting numerator before taking the limit.",
          "worked": "For $x>0$, combine the reciprocals in the numerator. Multiply by the conjugate so that the numerator becomes $x-(x+h)=-h$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x+h}}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}}{h}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{x+h}}{h\\sqrt{x+h}\\sqrt{x}}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{x-(x+h)}{h\\sqrt{x+h}\\sqrt{x}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{x+h})}\\\\f'(x)&=\\lim_{h\\to0}\\frac{-1}{\\sqrt{x+h}\\sqrt{x}(\\sqrt{x}+\\sqrt{x+h})}\\\\f'(x)&=-\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{x}}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      }
    ]
  },
